                                 <content>
                                    <AnchorPane minHeight="0.0" minWidth="0.0" prefHeight="180.0" prefWidth="200.0">
                                       <children>
                                          <Label alignment="TOP_LEFT" layoutX="14.0" layoutY="14.0" lineSpacing="7.0" prefHeight="190.0" prefWidth="554.0" text="Hope you completed your profile.&#10;&#10; 1. Go to Edit Previous CV Profiles.&#10; 2. Using pencil icon, CV Profile can be change again.&#10; 3. Select a template using report icon in the table.&#10; 4. Click on a template to get a preview of the CV.&#10; 5. Using print icon CV can convert to a PDF Format and download to your PC.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;" />
                                       </children>
                                    </AnchorPane>
                                 </content>
                              </TitledPane>
                              <TitledPane animated="false" collapsible="false" layoutX="23.0" layoutY="490.0" prefHeight="423.0" prefWidth="583.0" text="Tips for perfect resume / CV">
                                 <content>
                                    <AnchorPane minHeight="0.0" minWidth="0.0" prefHeight="180.0" prefWidth="200.0">
                                       <children>
                                          <Label alignment="TOP_LEFT" layoutX="14.0" layoutY="14.0" lineSpacing="7.0" prefHeight="361.0" prefWidth="554.0" text="How Resume content should be (General Rules)&#10;&#10; 1. Specific rather than general.&#10; 2. Active rather than passive language.&#10; 3. Written to express not impress.&#10; 4. Target for one page, if you have more experience go for 2 page.&#10; 5. Articulate rather than &quot;flowery&quot;.&#10; 6. Fact-based (quantify and qualify).&#10; 7. Make it easy to read and follow, balancing white space, well organized and concise.&#10; 8. Within headings, list information in reverse chronological order (most recent first).&#10; 9. Don't use personal pronouns (such as I).&#10;10. Don't use a narrative style.&#10;11. Don't use slang or colloquialisms.&#10;12. Include a picture unless you needed.&#10;13. Include age or gender.&#10;&#10;&#10;" />
                                       </children>
                                    </AnchorPane>
                                 </content>
                              </TitledPane>
